# FastAPI: Frontend, Backend aur API

## 1. Monolithic Architecture

Pehle applications ka frontend, backend, business logic aur database access aksar ek hi project ya codebase ka part hote the. Is architecture ko **monolithic architecture** kehte hain.

Example:

```text
User -> Monolithic Application -> Database
```

Monolith mein saari functionality ek hi application ke andar hoti hai:

- User interface
- Business logic
- Authentication
- Database operations
- Reports aur other features

### Monolithic architecture ki problems

- Frontend aur backend tightly coupled hote hain.
- Ek chhote change ke liye poori application ko build aur deploy karna pad sakta hai.
- Agar application ka critical part fail ho jaye, to poori application affect ho sakti hai.
- Application ko independently scale karna difficult hota hai.
- Ek hi codebase ko website, Android aur iPhone ke liye reuse karna difficult ho sakta hai.

Monolithic application hamesha galat nahi hoti. Chhote projects ke liye monolith simple aur useful ho sakta hai. Problems application ke bahut large aur tightly coupled hone par zyada clearly dikhai deti hain.

## 2. API ki Zarurat Kyon Padi?

API ka full form **Application Programming Interface** hai.

API ek controlled interface hai jiske through ek software doosre software se request aur response ke form mein communicate karta hai.

API ko public function ki tarah samajh sakte ho, lekin ye function generally network par available hota hai. Client ek URL ya endpoint ko request bhejta hai, aur server response return karta hai.

```text
Client -> API Endpoint -> Backend Logic -> Database or ML Model
Client <- JSON Response <- Backend Logic
```

### Important clarification

API sirf backend aur database ke beech ki layer nahi hoti. Usually API frontend ya kisi external client ko backend ki services provide karti hai.

Backend database se directly baat karta hai. Client ko database ka direct access nahi diya jata.

```text
Frontend -> API -> Backend -> Database
```

Is design mein database credentials aur internal business logic protected rehte hain.

## 3. API ke Benefits

### Controlled access

Client ko poore database ka access dene ke bajay sirf required operation ka access dete hain.

Example:

- Train search karna
- Flight availability check karna
- Ticket booking karna
- User profile dekhna
- Payment status check karna

IRCTC apna database directly MakeMyTrip ya kisi third-party application ko nahi dega. IRCTC controlled APIs provide kar sakta hai, jinke through authorized applications required data access karengi.

### Multiple clients support karna

Ek hi backend API ko multiple clients use kar sakte hain:

- Website
- Android application
- iPhone application
- Admin dashboard
- Third-party applications

```text
Website  ----\
Android  ----- > API -> Backend -> Database
iPhone   ----/
```

Isse har platform ke liye alag database logic likhne ki zarurat nahi padti.

### Security aur validation

Backend API request ko validate kar sakti hai:

- User authenticated hai ya nahi
- User ko requested resource ka permission hai ya nahi
- Input valid hai ya nahi
- User ko kitna data return karna hai

RBAC yani **Role-Based Access Control** ke through different users ko different permissions diye ja sakte hain.

## 4. API Endpoints

API endpoints specific URLs hote hain jo specific operations perform karte hain.

Example:

```text
GET  /trains
GET  /trains/123
POST /bookings
GET  /bookings/456
```

Har endpoint ke saath HTTP method aur request data define hota hai.

- `GET`: Data read karna
- `POST`: Naya data create karna
- `PUT` ya `PATCH`: Existing data update karna
- `DELETE`: Data remove karna

## 5. HTTP aur JSON

Frontend aur backend normally HTTP ya HTTPS protocol ke through communicate karte hain.

Request aur response mein data commonly JSON format mein bheja jata hai.

```json
{
  "train_number": "12345",
  "available_seats": 42,
  "status": "available"
}
```

JSON popular hai kyunki Java, Python, PHP, JavaScript aur other languages ise easily read aur generate kar sakti hain.

HTTPS use karne se communication encrypted hota hai. Authentication ke liye token, session ya OAuth jaise mechanisms use kiye ja sakte hain.

## 6. Multiple Platforms ka Example

Website, Android aur iPhone ke frontend alag technologies mein ban sakte hain:

- Website: HTML, CSS, JavaScript ya React
- Android: Kotlin ya Java
- iPhone: Swift

In teenon ka user interface alag ho sakta hai, lekin teeno same backend API ko call kar sakte hain.

```text
Website  ->
Android  -> API -> Common Backend -> Common Database
iPhone   ->
```

Is approach ke benefits:

- Business logic ek jagah maintain hota hai.
- Data consistency better hoti hai.
- Backend ko ek baar develop karke multiple platforms par use kar sakte hain.
- Authentication aur authorization centrally manage hoti hai.

Google, Uber, Zomato aur similar applications mein multiple clients common backend services ko use karte hain.

## 7. API aur Machine Learning Model

Machine learning application mein database ki jagah ya database ke saath trained ML model bhi backend service ka part ho sakta hai.

Model training ka general flow:

```text
Training Data -> Training Process -> Trained ML Model -> Saved Model File
```

Trained model ko file ke form mein save kiya ja sakta hai. Application start hone par backend model ko memory mein load karti hai.

Prediction flow:

```text
Frontend
	|
	| User query or input
	v
API Endpoint
	|
	v
Backend Prediction Function
	|
	v
Loaded ML Model
	|
	v
Prediction Result
	|
	v
JSON Response -> Frontend
```

Frontend model ko directly access nahi karti. Frontend API ko request bhejti hai, backend input validate karke model se prediction karwati hai, aur result JSON response ke roop mein return karti hai.

## 8. RAG System ka Example

RAG ka full form **Retrieval-Augmented Generation** hai.

Amazon jaise platform par user product ke baare mein question pooch sakta hai. RAG system relevant documents ya product information retrieve karke model ko context deta hai. Model us context ke basis par answer generate karta hai.

```text
User Query
	|
	v
API Endpoint
	|
	v
Backend
	|
	+-> Relevant Data Retrieve
	|
	+-> ML/LLM ko Context ke saath Request
	|
	v
Generated Answer
	|
	v
JSON Response -> Frontend
```

Model ko frontend par directly expose nahi kiya jata. API ke through access dene ke reasons hain:

- Model credentials aur internal details hide karna
- Request validation karna
- User permissions check karna
- Rate limiting apply karna
- Request aur response logging karna
- Model usage ka cost control karna

## 9. Recommendation System

Recommendation system bhi API ke through expose kiya ja sakta hai.

Example:

```text
Website / Android / iPhone
				|
				v
	  Recommendation API
				|
				v
 Backend + ML Model + User Data
				|
				v
 Recommended Products or Videos
```

Frontend user ke basis par recommendation API ko request bhejti hai. Backend user data, product data aur trained model ka use karke recommendations return karta hai.

## 10. FastAPI ka Role

FastAPI Python ka modern web framework hai jiska use APIs banane ke liye hota hai.

FastAPI ke through hum:

- API endpoints create kar sakte hain.
- Request data validate kar sakte hain.
- JSON responses return kar sakte hain.
- Database se connect kar sakte hain.
- ML model load karke prediction endpoint bana sakte hain.
- Automatic API documentation generate kar sakte hain.

Simple example:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()


@app.get("/hello")
def hello():
	 return {"message": "Hello from FastAPI"}
```

Is example mein `/hello` ek API endpoint hai. Client is endpoint ko call karega aur FastAPI JSON response return karega.

## Final Architecture

Modern application ka common structure kuch is tarah hota hai:

```text
Website / Android / iPhone
				  |
				  v
			 FastAPI
				  |
				  v
	 Backend Business Logic
			 /        \
			v          v
	 Database     ML/RAG Model
```

Short mein:

- Frontend user interface provide karta hai.
- API frontend aur backend ke beech communication ka interface hai.
- Backend business logic handle karta hai.
- Database data store karta hai.
- ML model prediction, generation ya recommendation karta hai.
- JSON data exchange ka common format hai.
- HTTP/HTTPS communication ka protocol hai.

Yahi approach industry mein websites, mobile applications, recommendation systems, prediction services aur AI applications deploy karne ke liye commonly use hoti hai.










